## Objective and scope

State the exact operation, environment, system, side effects, and exclusions.

<Warning>
  **HOLD — this template grants no operating authority.** Do not execute until the exact owner, authority envelope, credentials, provider scope, rollback, and evidence requirements are populated and approved.
</Warning>

## Authority and preconditions

| Predicate | Required state | Evidence/readback |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Owner and authority | Replace | Replace |
| Environment and target | Replace | Replace |
| Credential reference | Bound through approved custody | Never place a secret in this page |
| Backup/rollback | Verified target exists | Replace |
| Change window | Replace | Replace |
| Independent reviewer | Replace | Replace |

**STOP — do not continue** if any required predicate is absent, expired, ambiguous, or outside the approved scope.

## Inputs and protected-data boundary

- List exact public-safe identifiers and versions.
- Reference credentials by approved secret reference only.
- Identify restricted inputs that must remain outside Git, logs, screenshots, and documentation.
- State idempotency, concurrency, rate, and cost limits.

## Procedure

<Steps>
  <Step title="Freeze and identify the target">
    Record the exact environment, version, stable ID, current state, and rollback target.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Run preflight">
    Verify authority, dependencies, health, budget, evidence freshness, and stop conditions.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Execute the bounded action">
    Replace with exact instructions. Do not broaden the operation beyond the approved envelope.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Read back independently">
    Retrieve the resulting provider/runtime state and compare it with the expected assertion.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Reconcile and close">
    Record evidence, documentation impact, changelog, unresolved items, and the next inherited baseline.
  </Step>
</Steps>

## Verification and readback

| Assertion | Expected | Observed | Evidence | Verdict |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Replace | Replace | Replace | Replace | `PASS / FAILED / HOLD` |

**PASS — [exact assertion], [environment], [timestamp], [evidence reference].**

A syntax check, generated artifact, request dispatch, or `2xx` response is not enough when the operation requires provider readback, downstream fulfillment, settlement, entitlement, or independent verification.

## Failure and rollback

<Danger>
  **ROLLBACK REQUIRED — replace with the exact trigger and rollback target.** Preserve evidence before destructive recovery. If rollback cannot be verified, degrade to read-only or HOLD and escalate.
</Danger>

| Failure | Immediate containment | Retry rule | Rollback/compensation | Escalation |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Unknown mutation outcome | Stop writes | Do not replay blindly | Read current state first | Replace |
| Authorization/evidence failure | Fail closed | No retry until corrected | None | Replace |
| Readback mismatch | Quarantine result | Bounded diagnostic read only | Replace | Replace |

## Evidence and closure

Record:

- run, request, correlation, release, and evidence IDs;
- exact source and target versions;
- authority and reviewer;
- redacted request/response references;
- validation and readback results;
- rollback state;
- `docs_updated`, `docs_no_change`, or `docs_delta_opened`;
- unresolved holds and next review.

## Escalation

**FAILED — no PASS issued:** State the failed assertion, owner, severity, safe fallback, and exact evidence required.

